@packages/core/src/model/source.sigil import { SigilSourceModel }
@packages/core/src/model/diagnostics.sigil import { SigilDiagnosticModel }

component SigilRetrievalModel {
  goal {
    Define immutable purpose-retrieval targets, evidence, graphs, raw results, and
    agent-oriented projections.
  }

  interface {
    RetrievalModel {
      SigilSourceModel and SigilDiagnosticModel provide source and diagnostic data.

      PurposeRetrievalResult and its target, graph, evidence, inclusion, exclusion,
      context, and fingerprint data preserve deterministic retrieval output.
    }

    RetrievalProjection {
      RetrievalProjection is the separately versioned sigil-retrieval-projection/v1
      agent presentation schema derived deterministically from one
      PurposeRetrievalResult.

      RetrievalProjection preserves the raw sigil-purpose-retrieval/v1 result and its
      fingerprint without adding, removing, or reordering raw evidence.

      RetrievalProjection contains purpose, target, ordered RetrievedComponent
      entries, scoped diagnostics, and a projection fingerprint.

      RetrievedComponent has one stable component identity, path, selected,
      dependency, importer, cycle-member, or module-context role, component-owned
      links, and one purpose-appropriate contract projection.

      A component-owned link has one relation, an exact target component identity,
      and its available import or annotation location. Links do not require a
      separate presentation-level relationship map.

      A selected component contract groups goal, interface, constraints, decisions,
      and cases by their owning component. Its interface groups SemanticUnits by
      concept when a concept identity exists and retains ungrouped interface units
      without inventing a concept.

      A non-selected dependency contract exposes its goal and interface. A module
      context remains relationship context and does not repeat a component contract
      already represented by another RetrievedComponent.

      Matching expansion SemanticUnits merge into the owning component and matching
      concept or section. An expansion is not a presentation component, relationship
      category, or heading.

      OwnershipLink records an implements, uses, or tests relation, repository-
      relative implementation location, optional symbol, and selected sections. It
      belongs to its owning component or concept.

      Implementation-source evidence remains available only in the raw
      implementation-purpose result and is omitted from RetrievalProjection.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    RetrievalProjection {
      Projection component identities and links are exact, stable, and resolvable
      within the same projection.

      Projection ordering is deterministic: selected components first, then role,
      path, declaration location, and component name; links use relation, target
      identity, and available location; section units retain raw evidence order.

      Projection locations use normalized repository-relative paths and one-based
      line and column values already carried by raw retrieval evidence.

      A projection fingerprint covers its complete projection content and does not
      replace the raw PurposeRetrievalResult fingerprint.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    AgentRetrievalProjection {
      Decision: Preserve the evidence-first PurposeRetrievalResult v1 protocol and
      derive a separately versioned component-first retrieval projection for agents.

      Scope: Governs agent-facing retrieval data and Markdown rendering; excludes raw
      retrieval membership, evidence, graph, ordering, JSON Lines, and compiler
      report protocols.

      Trade-offs: The projection adds a maintained schema, but avoids making every
      host reconstruct component, concept, expansion, ownership, and link grouping.

      Design issues addressed: Flat evidence kinds expose expansions and source
      slices as peer content, producing repetitive Markdown that is difficult for
      people and agents to navigate.

      Discarded alternatives: Replacing raw v1 with a breaking grouped result and
      making every Markdown renderer infer groups from evidence were rejected.

      Consequences: Hosts can consume a stable grouped projection while automation
      retains the complete raw evidence result and its established fingerprint.

      Revisit when: A consumer requires a projection role, section, or relation that
      cannot be derived deterministically from purpose retrieval.
    }
  }

  cases {
    RetrievalProjection {
      A selected component with a MarkdownOutput concept groups its declaration and
      matching expansion interface units beneath MarkdownOutput without an expansion
      heading.

      A selected component exposes its constraints, decisions, and cases even when
      direct dependencies expose only their goal and interface.

      An ownership annotation for a selected concept becomes an OwnershipLink under
      that concept with the annotation's repository-relative line and column.

      An implementation-purpose raw result retains its selected source slices while
      the corresponding RetrievalProjection contains only OwnershipLinks.
    }
  }
}
